DESCRIPTION                   = "This table contains mineral abundances and
 analytical errors derived from diffraction-all K-alpha diffraction data for
 the Valle de la Luna drill sample, analyzed in CheMin cell number 11a
 (Mylar window). The analysis is based on RDA file
 CMB_814381120RDA46951191722CH00113P1. Mineral identifications, abundances
 and analytical errors for crystalline phases were determined using the
 program JADE. Mineral identification as Mg-sulfate.4H2O includes
 cranswickite and possibly starkeyite, which are two different forms of the
 4-hydrate. Both also occur intergrown at the type locality of cranswickite
 (Peterson 2011, Am. Min. 96, 869-877). High intensity in the low 2-theta
 region and a broad amorphous hump were modeled using FULLPAT to indicate
 that ~55 +/- 24 weight% of the total sample consists of X-ray amorphous
 materials. All errors cited are 2-sigma. Column 1 of the table lists
 mineral identifications, column 2 lists the Mineral abundances in weight
 percent, and column 3 indicates the estimated analytical errors."
END_OBJECT                    = SPREADSHEET
END

